One important technical correction

Your "mandatory stack" should be organized according to each algorithm's role:

ML-KEM (FIPS 203) → Quantum-resistant key establishment
ML-DSA (FIPS 204) (and optionally SLH-DSA (FIPS 205)) → Digital signatures
XChaCha20-Poly1305 or AES-256-GCM → High-speed symmetric encryption for files, databases, and network sessions
Argon2id → Password-based key derivation
BLAKE3 (or SHA-3 where required for compliance) → Hashing and integrity
HKDF → Session key derivation

This layered approach aligns with how modern cryptographic systems are designed.

